{{!--
  ToC panel (GH-10, Figma node 2610:27801/2686:47569 — "TABLE OF CONTENTS"
  renamed "On this page" per this issue's own decision). Deliberately no
  `.dt-grid-layout__item--span-*` utility class here: the split between
  this and article.hbs is gated behind `html.has-toc`, added by
  02-on-this-page.ts once it confirms there is a real ToC to show — see
  toc.css. A static utility class can't be conditional on that, and every
  page must render full width with JavaScript disabled (this issue's own
  acceptance criterion), so the grid math for both this and `.doc` lives
  in toc.css/doc.css instead of Handlebars.

  Sits first in `.content` (main.hbs) regardless of viewport: at m/l an
  explicit `grid-column-start` in toc.css puts it on the right of the
  article despite DOM order; at s/xs, where there is no docked column at
  all, DOM order alone is what stacks it above the article.
--}}
<aside id="on-this-page" class="toc" data-title="{{{or page.attributes.toctitle 'On this page'}}}" data-levels="{{{or page.attributes.toclevels 4}}}">
  <div class="toc-menu"></div>
</aside>
